deviations higher than the overall mean across the 13 other nations. So yes, in principle, external threat can bring us apart. In practice, maybe the Chinese army has to make it all the way to Omaha and then we'll finally pull together because the threats that we've seen, 9-11 and COVID, they don't seem to be anywhere close to big enough. Are Democrats and Republicans equally polarized? Your paper gauges how different groups regard each other on a feeling thermometer. So are there temperature differences between Democrats and Republicans? Generally no. So the feeling thermometer, as some of your listeners may know, is a scale from zero to one. 100 where zero is cold and 100 is warm and you can evaluate, you know, if you're a Democrat,

